# Nouns that count people or things a clock never takes: a bare hour behind a
# clock preposition and directly before one of them is a count ("wave at 5
# people").  Each word is quoted from its Wiktionary Noun entry
# (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the fetched pages are kept with the audit.
# personnes: Noun. "plural of personne"
# invités: Noun. "plural of invité"
# voisins: Noun. "plural of voisin"
# voisines: Noun. ""
# amis: Noun. "plural of ami"
# amies: Noun. "plural of amie"
# enfants: Noun. "plural of enfant"
# joueurs: Noun. "plural of joueur"
# places: Noun. "plural of place"
# tables: Noun. "plural of table"
# billets: Noun. "plural of billet"
# chambres: Noun. "plural of chambre"
# euros: Noun. "plural of euro"
personnes
invités
voisins
voisines
amis
amies
enfants
joueurs
places
tables
billets
chambres
euros
